- F-58 **Under the compiled checker against today's one library, microGPT's flat program, C4, has 42 distinct error sites of its own, 23 of them the index bound that its helpers do not write; each count is a floor.** By the distance stage's driver on `832f7d0d91`: `FlatArrays` 31, `FlatData` 3, `MicroGptFlat` 8. In `FlatArrays`, 23 are 'The static argument I does not satisfy the corresponding bound Index' in seven generic declarations (P-156); `model-closure-check.md` lists the other 8. `MicroGptFlat`'s 8 are `DOT`, `view` and `gather` on unsized arrays, one `if` of pairs, and line 82's `1.0 s`, a float numeral beside a `ZZ32` value which that tree's checker left tied between `RR64`'s and `QQ`'s product, as it left `MicroGptFlatQuick.fss:40`. The numeral powers pass. The APL program's four files hold 54 sites, and its grammar's api crashes the checker. No run has counted the sites since `832f7d0d91`, and two changes of the checker move `MicroGptFlat`'s. It now takes both numeral lines at `RR64`'s product (F-366). It now types the names of a top-level tuple binding, and lines 17 to 19 compile (F-369): by one run of that change alone, line 41's `if` of pairs is no longer a site, and line 77's `beta1 m`, an `RR64` times an unsized array, is a new one. In a scratch tree whose compile command selects the one library (F-352), with `I extends Index` written in the helpers and `gather`'s bound widened in a copy, the compile command reports 17, 15 of them the model's static types, its arrays without sizes (P-87). The checker stops a block at its first failing statement, so each count is a floor. Measured once each; no test checks it. Command: `compile-ladder/plan-31/probes/model-closure/run.sh check`. Detail: `compile-ladder/plan-31/probes/model-closure-check.md`, "1. The counts"; `compile-ladder/plan-31/probes/switch-rehearsal.md`, "microGPT's flat program"; `compile-ladder/rung-tuple-binding/REPORT.md`, "Programs run old against new".
