- F-78 **The compiled checker instantiates a type parameter that nothing at a call fixes at the intersection of its upper bounds, never `BottomType`, and tries a call by subtyping without the expected type first.** It builds P-48 and P-49. Where the call has an expected type, its attempts come in this order: subtyping without the expected type, kept when its result converts to it; subtyping with the expected type; coercion with it; and coercion without it. The second lets a call whose untyped function argument only the expected type fixes type-check, since the coercion attempt cannot check such an argument (row 507). P-49 decides the first and the third; the second and the fourth are an agent's choice, the instance-bound rung's (its decision record, D4). An argument of intersection type fixes a parameter at the whole intersection, not at one conjunct (row 541). The run time has no class for an intersection type, so such an instance dies as it loads (row 559). Gated by `compiler_tests/InferResultOnly*` and `InferContextKeepsFit`. Detail: `compile-ladder/rung-instance-bound/REPORT.md` sections 1 and 7; the order, by reading, `compile-ladder/rung-instance-bound/decision-record.md`, D4, and `scala_src/typechecker/impls/Functionals.scala:962-966`.
